{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0983bbf29b4045e2d726bd156f2c8ae292df3a38e4410c80b6029ca6347f58f7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_050a0f1356d2f8c1c539c010a6d22550c12313012c96543fefdfea4189e52424","slc_9aea4e27e380985041a6647916d771d2e523c280a77d635ae4c4753babcd9aab"],"source_ids":["src_980c78f9cbf456a4be1b45d98936912c"],"text":"An OpenMultiAgent instance is constructed with a default provider/model and an onToolCall callback that can return 'suspend' for consequential tool calls or 'allow' otherwise.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_138096f7ff345494150fc199d68913fe2f5b3035c23c5be92471c5b4854c1609","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1e94ae25144d12ec74ff434afc7ee739552e40b7b82d0b1f8e9598e2519b2a0d"],"source_ids":["src_c8ceca53380f583fad5fb8741540c0d8"],"text":"When maxTurns is reached the run stops before the next model call and is still reported successful with no distinguishing flag; the docs suggest comparing toolCalls or message counts, or setting a lower maxTurns and treating a long run as an alert.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_21575bcd943e015a5692e0b3247855243cf04e1a986d2bda6ed4ea7103614b72","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_82e119225ef5f47dfc5c35025356523516f0eef1ea2f2159f02463235a5e8fae","slc_c2061ca00a2400bd2c94a867f7343de007e757abe57dcab8bce32675fdc7eda7","slc_d2784b0282216a312f88143972f425bb372a23b664b5d97e8b9a4a08a82315ac"],"source_ids":["src_c852aafddd21500bbbd91f2264cafb06"],"text":"Patch operations are addTasks, retargetPending, and supersedePending; started or terminal tasks cannot be retargeted or superseded, and repairs are forward-only with no undo of external side effects.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_22d61fd874fb6916074dfc80070a3ba9bba39877dc3123c94ccef49116297ee9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_03d7024f94d20a90df230927ce5c3bda2546883fe11425c5dfe5fe0fcce30040"],"source_ids":["src_980c78f9cbf456a4be1b45d98936912c"],"text":"Repository development practice: issues and pull requests are welcome, with CONTRIBUTING.md covering workspace boundaries, validation, and submission guidance.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4a6d50386ec2f86137b83748c2588be1b36378f8848e55907c76fa8ec401a4ba","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_abed82579077248c3af159ab3caed2bd5e6c80d5223b3ad8b5f13e3eac6de40e"],"source_ids":["src_980c78f9cbf456a4be1b45d98936912c"],"text":"Egress policy supports 'offline' or 'allowlist' modes checked before a built-in adapter connects; child policies can only tighten parents, unenforceable transports fail closed, and process/ACP backends sit outside the policy.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5a194948e06165e8044e794a22cdcac4add585894c6760c4df609e0587f23b2a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3f52574ee8d54763780b8b359132618ec821f397ed22535a1df021e673f28c9a"],"source_ids":["src_980c78f9cbf456a4be1b45d98936912c"],"text":"With governanceIntent 'required', runs are judged on an execution receipt of roles, ordering, dependency edges, and independent review; the evaluator never sees agent output text, and a successful run can still report 'unsatisfied'.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5d4577bb8e47f59b43b6c9e29ce955b3c5f2dcd3ada059091118a36dc69dae12","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4088d2979ed3c9f8c015c9c7f8609a5d2f588783eb55346fcfe8a872cd9175cf"],"source_ids":["src_980c78f9cbf456a4be1b45d98936912c"],"text":"The runtime records every model block, tool call, and context rewrite in a journal; verifyRun() checks offline that each block reproduces byte for byte, reporting evicted windows as inconclusive rather than failures.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6ee9ffd4d6d73ead1fc400701983c223c8b139a5b2358d68a627471c3ff5829d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_38820bcfabd8b8e95ce3aca803d1ab6c55b9ce921dcd8df0111cc388181b6937"],"source_ids":["src_980c78f9cbf456a4be1b45d98936912c"],"text":"Consequential actions pause for durable approvals: a suspend request is stored beside the checkpoint, bound to a SHA-256 hash of what the reviewer saw, decisions are atomic and first-wins, and tampered requests fail closed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_85dc8b1c6fe8d4e2b05fbfb52921da3814ef25bba8c39ff4dedcc4101760d8b1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_efb04ebce4bc2166e34aca905a975907184f235ab78e8095ed3a29e3555e13bb","slc_fb90112f22868fe47a51e46759f81da9ffd93fef735df5efca1c1fd58cba289e"],"source_ids":["src_c852aafddd21500bbbd91f2264cafb06"],"text":"Adaptive recovery is opt-in via recovery.mode 'repairable': a Replanner or onTaskOutcome callback proposes a PlanPatch, OMA validates it, an optional onPlanPatch gate approves it, and the patch is applied atomically before the triggering task completes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9f8c09e23b31b6a7fb4aff90a02b34b539773ad5c9b8b2bd71b8c6301498ee75","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e5ea24f2c70526d04d536c4234f3197abd7ea6fef6d267709eae10896601641a"],"source_ids":["src_980c78f9cbf456a4be1b45d98936912c"],"text":"runTeam() uses one model call to turn a goal into a task graph with assignees and dependencies, a deterministic scheduler executes it, and a second call writes the final answer; the coordinator is not consulted mid-run.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_af0fe9f9166a6e7b9c2f52fa9a919e46a1c8857e668601461f3ca209cc1af38c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b45198ba6997d232b3dc7f8437035247e9578de178041ea04e224e68fbe16c7a"],"source_ids":["src_980c78f9cbf456a4be1b45d98936912c"],"text":"The project requires Node.js 20 or newer; Node 20 is upstream-EOL, kept only as a migration window, and will be removed in the next major release no earlier than 2026-10-31.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b6db8eaf021a8a578de9f07c29be4e9c4f173f63707086d01ea18bfd1aa0af2f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_abed82579077248c3af159ab3caed2bd5e6c80d5223b3ad8b5f13e3eac6de40e"],"source_ids":["src_980c78f9cbf456a4be1b45d98936912c"],"text":"Built-in provider adapters cover Anthropic, OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, Bedrock, Gemini, Grok, Copilot, several Chinese providers, plus Ollama, vLLM, and llama-server via baseURL and any OpenAI-compatible or Vercel AI SDK endpoint.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e9f03b5b2fbd135e331d6f0c3345c39ab4ec6124de05e87ad26caab4eed37c09","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c490a9048e9c9563502536c57f1bf023abf841242d33717c973265d1b667ec8a"],"source_ids":["src_c8ceca53380f583fad5fb8741540c0d8"],"text":"Budgets are checked only at turn and task boundaries, so a run can overshoot its ceiling by up to one model turn; exhausting a budget is reported via a budget_exceeded event and result fields rather than thrown.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ffe8d231e17839decbf44cf7b6d6a4d2a535b68f0dd2b8ead70800d65e63db5a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"open-multi-agent/open-multi-agent@eaeb420c4364 snapshot fccf7ae5c773ed7e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_752554f46bbfef0c27bc2f6259c3145ca4e4774a47531cbbc3c545ca2782117f"],"source_ids":["src_980c78f9cbf456a4be1b45d98936912c"],"text":"The core package exposes three run modes: runAgent() for a single agent, runTasks() for an explicit pipeline, and runTeam() which plans from a goal.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:26:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_860178ba4c194ce28586ca49914e10c8"}
